 shaping controls.",["Notes"]],["Microfreak/Preset/370%20TMF.24.11.23.D/","source-block-556","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/370%20TMF.24.11.23.D/","source-block-566","An archived GitP.24.11.23.D.mfpz patch contains this preset name. It shares its stored digital oscillator Type, two oscillator parameter fields, and filter resonance with the archived Microfreak/Preset/369 TMF.24.11.23.C patch; the remaining oscillator field and filter cutoff differ. The saved Type is one setting, while Microfreak/UG/06 Dig Osc/02 Param Controls notes that Type can also be modulated during playback.",["Notes"]],["Microfreak/Preset/371%20TMF.24.11.25.A/","source-block-560","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/372%20TMF.24.11.25.B/","source-block-560","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/373%20TMF.24.11.25.C/","source-block-560","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/374%20TMF.24.12.04.A/","source-block-560","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/375%20TMF.24.12.04.B/","source-block-560","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/376%20TMF.24.12.04.C/","source-block-560","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/377%20TMF.24.12.04.D/","source-block-550","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/378%20Anit/","source-block-535","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/379%20Bnit/","source-block-526","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/380%20Cnit/","source-block-530","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/381%20Dnit/","source-block-527","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/382%20Anit/","source-block-530","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/384%20Bnit/","source-block-530","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/385%20Cnit/","source-block-530","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/386%20Dnit/","source-block-525","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/387%20Enit/","source-block-531","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/388%20Anit1/","source-block-527","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/389%20Bnit2/","source-block-533","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/390%20Cnit2/","source-block-533","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/391%20Dnit2/","source-block-532","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/392%20Blithrifi/","source-block-539","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/393%20answ%20er/","source-block-540","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/394%20Jing%20A/","source-block-539","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/395%2026.06.25/","source-block-536","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/396%20Anit/","source-block-534","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/397%20Imit/","source-block-488","Notes",[]],["Microfreak/Preset/397%20Imit/","source-block-498","Used in a recent episode; the episode association is unspecified.",["Notes"]],["Microfreak/Preset/397%20Imit/","source-block-576","Saved patch download and export: Microfreak/CLI/Validation/26-10-03 slot 397.",["Notes"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-108","MicroFreak User Guide",[]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-134","The MicroFreak user guide documents the instrument and its controls.",["MicroFreak User Guide"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-206","Sections",["MicroFreak User Guide"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-221","Microfreak/UG/01 Welcome and Introduction",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-271","Microfreak/UG/02 Installation",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-309","Microfreak/UG/03 Overview",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-343","Microfreak/UG/04 Presets",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-376","Microfreak/UG/05 Connections",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-413","Microfreak/UG/06 Dig Osc",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-446","Microfreak/UG/07 Filter",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-478","Microfreak/UG/08 LFO",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-507","Microfreak/UG/09 Envelope Gen",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-545","Microfreak/UG/10 Keyboard",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-579","Microfreak/UG/11 Icon Strip",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-615","Microfreak/UG/12 Arpeggiator",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-652","Microfreak/UG/13 Sequencer",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-687","Microfreak/UG/14 Config",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-719","Microfreak/UG/15 Using Scales",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-757","Microfreak/UG/16 Paraphonic Chord Mode",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-804","Microfreak/UG/17 Ext Gear",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-838","Microfreak/UG/18 Appendix A Speech Osc",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-885","Microfreak/UG/19 Appendix B Vocoder",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-929","Microfreak/UG/20 Appendix C - Cheat Sheet",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-979","Microfreak/UG/21 Appendix D - CC Values",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-1027","Microfreak/UG/22 Declaration of Conformity",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/","source-block-1078","Microfreak/UG/23 Software License Agreement",["MicroFreak User Guide","Sections"]],["Microfreak/UG/01%20Welcome%20and%20Introduction/","source-block-134","01 Welcome and Introduction",[]],["Microfreak/UG/01%20Welcome%20and%20Introduction/","source-block-166","Congratulations on your purchase of the Arturia MicroFreak!",["01 Welcome and Introduction"]],["Microfreak/UG/01%20Welcome%20and%20Introduction/","source-block-229","The MicroFreak is a compact, versatile, semi-modular synthesizer with many distinctive features. It lets you experiment with modular sound construction without patch cords.",["01 Welcome and Introduction"]],["Microfreak/UG/01%20Welcome%20and%20Introduction/","source-block-405","The standard MicroFreak and MicroFreak Vocoder Edition share the instrument's core features. The Vocoder Edition has a white casing and a gooseneck microphone; see Microfreak/UG/19 Appendix B Vocoder for its specific features.",["01 Welcome and Introduction"]],["Microfreak/UG/01%20Welcome%20and%20Introduction/","source-block-639","Its digital oscillator and analog filter combine a broad range of digital sounds with a warm analog character. A cycling envelope adds modulation options associated with high-end modular systems, and the modulation matrix routes sources to many destinations.",["01 Welcome and Introduction"]],["Microfreak/UG/01%20Welcome%20and%20Introduction/","source-block-901","The pressure-sensitive touch keyboard, paraphonic playing, arpeggiator, and assignable modulation destinations make the MicroFreak suited to expressive performance.",["01 Welcome and Introduction"]],["Microfreak/UG/01%20Welcome%20and%20Introduction/","source-block-1069","The MicroFreak is a USB MIDI Class Compliant device and can connect to compatible devices without installing drivers. Connecting an iPad may require a camera connection or USB-to-Lightning cable.",["01 Welcome and Introduction"]],["Microfreak/UG/01%20Welcome%20and%20Introduction/","source-block-1268","Two paraphonic sequencers can record and play up to four voices at once, sharing one filter; each sequencer has four modulation tracks.",["01 Welcome and Introduction"]]],"format_version":2}